Description:

Cyrus now refuses to send mail whose envelope sender or recipient could end
the SMTP command it's written in: control characters anywhere, or a space,
angle bracket, quote or backslash outside a quoted local-part.  Previously a
CalDAV or JMAP calendar attendee address with a percent-encoded CRLF was
written into RCPT TO verbatim, letting any calendar user inject SMTP
commands, including a whole second message with an envelope of their
choosing.  iMIP also no longer sends to, or lists in invitations, attendees
with such addresses.


